{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-server/src/shell/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:04:06.182267Z","id":"5449351ce4ddaf89b99e33a17e7c694528b9a2ecd070eab04731f3d6c9263498","body":{"detail":"TRANSPORT_SCRIPT (crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs:398) names /_clax/transport.js with no version, and static_file's fallback branch serves it with `public, max-age=3600` and no ETag (only mark.svg and mark-dot.svg otherwise land here; the bridge is ?v=<hash>, shell/ and bridge/ files are content-hashed, the contract's .d.ts are no-cache). The shell document itself is private, no-cache. While the app reaches the embedded core over loopback (until plan Task 15's scheme handler), the WebView's HTTP cache keeps the script across app and bundle updates: after an update that changes the transport's receivers (2da5051b4 moved the nonce to the first argument of callResult/streamBlock/streamEnd), the old cached script reads callResult(nonce, id, r) as callResult(id, r), finds no call, and every API call and the event stream hang for up to an hour. Content-hashing beats no-cache here: the script is parser-blocking in <head>, and no-cache would add a revalidation round trip to every shell document load (time to usable), while a versioned URL in a no-cache document is always current.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":353},"content_hash":"c5127f4323a62c1928e32914480972fc9fa32a3f05cd2dc89e74b93295595947"},"suggested_fix":"Serve it as the bridge is served: write <script src=\"/_clax/transport.js?v=<short_hash of its sha256>\"> in with_embed_meta (bridge_version's shape over web.sha256(\"_clax/transport.js\")), answer IMMUTABLE at the matching v and REVALIDATE with an ETag otherwise (bridge_cache_control generalised), and pin both in crates/clax-server/tests/shell_boot.rs.","summary":"/_clax/transport.js is served unversioned with public, max-age=3600 and no ETag, so a WebView over loopback can run an hour-old transport against a newer relay","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
